      "commentary": {
        "title": "What moves the market",
        "points": [
          "**Discount** grows 7.8% a year on price-sensitive households, who have been trading down across all categories since the energy shock and now visit discounters at least once a week in most regions",
          "**Online** is still small but compounding at 14% a year, driven by quick-commerce in the two largest metropolitan areas and by subscription models from the pure players",
          "**Supermarkets** grow at 2%, below food inflation, which means volumes are shrinking in real terms for the first time in a decade",
          "**Hypermarkets** shrink as shopping trips move to proximity formats, and several operators are converting out-of-town boxes",
          "**Convenience** keeps growing at 5% thanks to food-to-go, although margins are under pressure from waste"
        ]
      },
      "source": "National statistics; retailer reports; team market model (illustrative)"
